# Siya bots — naming freeze + Assist product alignment

## Frozen labels (do not blur)

| Label | Product | Audience | Code today |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| **External bot** | Siya Guide | Patients / public site | `apps/siya-assistant` → [siya-guide.vercel.app](https://siya-guide.vercel.app) |
| **Internal bot** | Siya Assist | Staff help desk | Internal Siya OS / `docs/siyaos-knowledge-base/` |

Full freeze: `docs/BOT-NAMING-FREEZE.md`.

If a request says “assistant” without qualifying, **ask** which bot: external (Guide) or internal (Assist).

## What we are building (Internal bot)

**Siya Assist** = one internal **AI help desk** with routing: intent → department → task-specific follow-ups → approved KB → action or escalation with context.

**Not:** ERP, EMR, SAP-style modules, dashboard suite, 74-category nested menus, or “company handbook” as the primary UX.

**Not:** the patient-facing website chatbot (that is the **External bot / Guide**).

## Before implementing a user or pasted spec, ask (in chat) when any of these apply

1. **Which bot?** — External (Guide) vs Internal (Assist) is ambiguous.
2. **Scope** — Adds dashboards, CRUD admin, project management, or multi-app navigation instead of **one chat + escalation**.
3. **Taxonomy** — More than **~8 routing departments** for v1 without explicit approval.
4. **Clinical/legal** — Bot makes clinical, legal, or refund **decisions** instead of SOP + escalate.
5. **Knowledge** — Ingesting unapproved Drive dumps without metadata (owner, status, roles, review date).
6. **Naming** — Conflicts with patient-facing **Siya Guide** / External bot, or public site KB governance.
7. **Duplicate philosophy** — Re-documenting what already lives in `apps/siya-health/brand/` or governance v1.0 instead of **linking + retrieval**.

Use **AskQuestion** or a short numbered list when the request is ambiguous. Do not silently build the enterprise version.

## Approved v1 departments (Internal bot routing only)

Accounts · HR · Marketing · Clinical Operations · Compliance · Technology · Leadership · General

## Knowledge layers (do not merge)

| Layer | Path | Use |
|-------|------|-----|
| Internal help desk KB | `docs/siyaos-knowledge-base/` | Staff + **Internal bot (Assist)** |
| Patient/public graph | `apps/siya-health/` + governance + Public Knowledge API | Website + **External bot (Guide)** |

## Assist / staff portal (reminder)

Staff help desk = **one chat + escalation** primary. Executive Workspace is an **orientation/decision lane** on My day for founders — not a second product and not an ERP. Build against `apps/hipaa-training/docs/EXECUTIVE-WORKSPACE-v2-FOUNDER-DECISION-COACH.md` when touching that lane.

## MVP checklist — Internal bot (prefer this order)

Login (optional) → one prompt → router → follow-ups → retrieval + sources → escalate with collected context → admin upload (later).

## Example pushback (copy tone)

> “That sounds like an operations module inside an ERP. For the **Internal bot (Assist)** v1 we’d route this to **Accounts → Reimbursement**, ask amount/date/receipt/approval, then pull an approved policy—or escalate with a filled summary. Want that flow added to the KB instead of a new app screen?”
